{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_014Pc7DJPoSk5tdhX4hWfbEa", "type": "tool_result", "content": "Web search results for query: \"TinyStories\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2305.07759\"},{\"title\":\"hyper.ai\",\"url\":\"https://hyper.ai/en/datasets/33032\"},{\"title\":\"www.huggingface.co\",\"url\":\"https://www.huggingface.co/datasets/roneneldan/TinyStories/blob/main/README.md?code=true\"},{\"title\":\"huggingface.co\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/roneneldan/TinyStories\"},{\"title\":\"Multilingual TinyStories: A Synthetic Combinatorial Corpus of Indic Children's Stories for Training Small Language Models\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.14563\"},{\"title\":\"TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?\",\"url\":\"https://deepai.org/publication/tinystories-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak-coherent-english\"},{\"title\":\"TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?\",\"url\":\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/?p=973236\"},{\"title\":\"Loading Events\",\"url\":\"https://www.math.harvard.edu/event/the-tinystories-dataset-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak-coherent-english/\"},{\"title\":\"Loading Events\",\"url\":\"https://cmsa.fas.harvard.edu/event/nt-92023\"},{\"title\":\"TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent\\\\n English?\",\"url\":\"https://liner.com/ko/review/tinystories-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak\"},{\"title\":\"tinystories small language models that still speak coherent\",\"url\":\"https://www.alignmentforum.[scrubbed:long-base64]\"},{\"title\":\"Quick review\",\"url\":\"https://liner.com/review/tinystories-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak\"},{\"title\":\"tinystories 4ce620e569a4\",\"url\":\"https://cobusgreyling.medium.com/tinystories-4ce620e569a4\"},{\"title\":\"hyper.ai\",\"url\":\"https://hyper.ai/cn/datasets/33032\"},{\"title\":\"The Tiny Model Revolution with Ronen Eldan and Yuanzhi Li of Microsoft Research\",\"url\":\"https://cognitiverevolution.ai/the-tiny-model-revolution-with-ronen-eldan-and-yuanzhi-li-of-microsoft-research\"},{\"title\":\"Source code for oumi.datasets.pretraining.tiny_stories\",\"url\":\"https://oumi.ai/docs/en/latest/_modules/oumi/datasets/pretraining/tiny_stories.html\"},{\"title\":\"www.alphaxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.alphaxiv.org/overview/2504.09184\"},{\"title\":\"🚀NEW COURSEVibe Coding AI Apps with Claude Code 🤖✨Enroll now\",\"url\":\"https://academy.dair.ai/papers/tinystories\"},{\"title\":\"Go backThe blogThis article\",\"url\":\"https://sfcompute.com/blog/tiny-narrations\"},{\"title\":\"meilu.jpshuntong.com\",\"url\":\"https://meilu.jpshuntong.com/url-68747470733a2f2f61727869762e6f7267/pdf/2305.07759.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"www.wizwand.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.wizwand.com/dataset/tinystories\"}]\n\nTinyStories is a synthetic dataset of short stories from Microsoft Research, introduced in a 2023 paper by Ronen Eldan and Yuanzhi Li. It was built to train and test small language models. The stories use only vocabulary a 3- to 4-year-old would likely understand, and they were generated with GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 generated by GPT-3.5 and GPT-4.\n\nKey points from the results:\n\n- **Purpose:** The dataset is used to train and evaluate models with under 10 million parameters, aiming for fluent, consistent narratives (training and evaluating SLMs (below 10 million parameters) to produce fluent and consistent narratives).\n- **Versions:** A later release, TinyStoriesV2-GPT4, uses only GPT-4 generations, since the original's GPT-3.5 stories are of lower quality (based on generations by GPT-4 only).\n- **Availability:** It is hosted on Hugging Face under the roneneldan/TinyStories name, and the dataset is available under the CDLA-Sharing-1.0 license.\n- **Criticism:** A later ETH Zürich project, SimpleStories, argues the dataset is repetitive. 59% of TinyStories samples began with the formulaic phrase \"Once upon a time,\"\n- **Derivatives:** Others have built on it, including a multilingual Indic version and a synthetic audio version from sfcompute.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "2f037402-1e87-48fa-bd95-84c4b0bb4372", "uuid": "fa081a96-f757-437b-98e2-5d6555e30b87", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T17:19:08.493Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "TinyStories", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_012qWBhzwc1re1bsfgr2dwax", "content": [{"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2305.07759"}, {"title": "hyper.ai", "url": "https://hyper.ai/en/datasets/33032"}, {"title": "www.huggingface.co", "url": "https://www.huggingface.co/datasets/roneneldan/TinyStories/blob/main/README.md?code=true"}, {"title": "huggingface.co", "url": "https://huggingface.co/datasets/roneneldan/TinyStories"}, {"title": "Multilingual TinyStories: A Synthetic Combinatorial Corpus of Indic Children's Stories for Training Small Language Models", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.14563"}, {"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?", "url": "https://deepai.org/publication/tinystories-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak-coherent-english"}, {"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?", "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/?p=973236"}, {"title": "Loading Events", "url": "https://www.math.harvard.edu/event/the-tinystories-dataset-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak-coherent-english/"}, {"title": "Loading Events", "url": "https://cmsa.fas.harvard.edu/event/nt-92023"}, {"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and S